// Translate in place: replace the //RS lines below with the 1:1 Jet port (keep `// Rust: <file>:<line>` anchors).
//RS //! D-MIGRATE1 / D-MIGRATE2 (ratified 2026-06-22): sema diff pass for
//RS //! `#PublishedSchema` structs.
//RS //!
//RS //! After struct registration, for each `#PublishedSchema` struct:
//RS //! 1. Load the prior snapshot from `.jet/cache/schema/<TypeName>.snapshot` (if any).
//RS //! 2. Diff old vs new field layout (keyed by name, so field *order* is ignored —
//RS //!    D-MIGRATE2F: reordering is never a breaking change).
//RS //! 3. Collect declared `migration <Type> { … }` ops for this type.
//RS //! 4. Refuse a breaking data-shape change unless a migration declares the intent:
//RS //!    - a field removed from old, not bridged by `rename old -> new` or `remove old`;
//RS //!    - a field whose type changed, not bridged by a `change f: Old -> New [via …]`;
//RS //!    - a field added in the new shape that old data can't supply (no `add` op).
//RS //!    Every such case is the single umbrella code E0910 with case-specific text.
//RS //! 5. Validate the declared ops against reality too (e.g. `remove f` where `f`
//RS //!    still exists, `add f` where `f` isn't actually new), so a nonsensical
//RS //!    migration teaches rather than silently passing.
//RS //!
//RS //! D-MIGRATE4 (ratified 2026-07-03): the runtime half lives in two places —
//RS //! `desugar_migrations` below rewrites `via { … }` converters and `add`
//RS //! defaults into synthetic top-level functions (type-checked and lowered
//RS //! through the normal pipeline), and codegen
//RS //! (`Codegen/Items.rs::emit_struct_migration`) emits per-block step functions
//RS //! plus a silent migration chain-walker for each decodable
//RS //! `#PublishedSchema` type with migration blocks.
//RS //!
//RS //! I3: all checking here; codegen only performs the mechanical lowering.
//RS 
